 "session": "59GEMSDOE / arena/ddbdbb81-59gemsdoe (Session H59-I2)",
 "lane": "Intensity: zone by new-fault density, then tile only what clears break-even",
 "hypothesis": "H59-I2 (LOCO Two-Host Structural + Geophysical + QFaults Effort Presence-Only IPP with De-Wrapped Cross-Block Corridor Utility Tiling): Replacing Session H59-I's non-structural 13-feature GLM and wrapping modulo-10 block lattice with a Leave-One-Component-Out (LOCO) two-host presence-only MaxEnt/Poisson point process over 31 covariates (10 geophysical edge/regime/scarp planes, 6 self-component-subtracted density & joined USGS/INGENIOUS QFaults FCODE2023/MAPSCALE effort planes, and 15 two-host quadratic log-distance, stepover facing/ratio, and host-bend curvature planes), zoned into 1 km blocks at the 1.5% break-even threshold and tiled across the 3.5 km structural corridor with the holdout-derived utility table ({q1_low: none, q2: 4px, q3: 4px, q4_high: 3px}), doubles Session H59-I holdout DTI and beats the published all-lane holdout best (0.135204).",
 "mechanism": "Leave-One-Component-Out (LOCO) two-host Euclidean distance transform (two_host_frame + cKDTree on visible catalogue only) assigns every visible catalogue pixel its true inter-component distance d1 <- d(x, C2(x)) ([10,50,90]% = [3.16, 9.00, 29.97] px) and secondary host d2 <- d(x, C3(x)), eliminating the d=0 self-distance degeneracy (IR-59-LOCO-01) and self-strand effort density leakage (IR-59-LOCO-EFFORT). Case-control Poisson/MaxEnt GLM (Fithian & Hastie 2013; Phillips et al. 2009) fitted strictly on visible presences vs target-group background (3 < d1 <= 35 px) predicts continuous intensity lambda(x); summing lambda(x) over non-catalogue corridor pixels inside each 1 km x 1 km block yields expected new-fault density n_b. Blocks clearing break-even (n_b >= 1.5 px, with q1_low pruned by the utility table so effective break-even is the q25 threshold ~2.0 px = 2% block density) are tiled by greedy 2D triangular-kernel expected-reward maximization (E[w_300m * lambda]) with cross-block spacing enforcement ({q2: 4px, q3: 4px, q4_high: 3px}), fixing Session H59-I's modulo-10 wraparound collision bug (IR-59-LATTICE-MOD10).",
 "named_non_fault_mimic": "Mapping-effort bias and topographic/geophysical non-fault lineaments: 1:24,000/1:100,000 quadrangle boundaries, road-corridor mapping density, non-tectonic fluvial terrace risers and erosional range-front scarps in 3DEP detrended elevation, and aeromagnetic flight-line levelling residuals or pluton-margin gravity gradients that parallel nearby mapped faults without brittle shear offset.",
